# Belgium: art. XII.6 WER (additions to data/extracted/be/).

lg:BE-WER
    eli:title "Wetboek van economisch recht"@nl , "Code de droit économique"@fr , "Code of Economic Law"@en ;
    lgo:shortName "WER / CDE" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2000-31 ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2013-11 ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. XII.6 (inserted by W 2013-12-15/51, in force 31.05.2014) asks for the ondernemingsnummer rather than a named register (4°) and keeps the Directive's codes-of-conduct item (8°)."@en .

lg:BE-CSA
    eli:title "Wetboek van vennootschappen en verenigingen"@nl ;
    eli:title "Code des sociétés et des associations"@fr ;
    lgo:shortName "WVV/CSA" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2017-1132 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.ejustice.just.fgov.be/eli/wet/2019/03/23/2019A40586/justel> ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 2:20 applies the company-law disclosure list to websites as well as deeds, invoices, letters and order forms. It goes beyond Directive 2017/1132 art. 26: the enterprise number is always required, and the e-mail address and the company's own website are required when the document shows them. Art. 2:21 makes a quoted capital the paid-up capital per the last balance sheet."@en .

# Belgium: art. 10/2 of the Wet van 30 juli 2018 (additions to data/extracted/be/).

lg:BE-GBW
    eli:title "Wet van 30 juli 2018 betreffende de bescherming van natuurlijke personen met betrekking tot de verwerking van persoonsgegevens"@nl ;
    eli:title "Loi du 30 juillet 2018 relative à la protection des personnes physiques à l'égard des traitements de données à caractère personnel"@fr ;
    eli:title "Law of 30 July 2018 on the protection of natural persons with regard to the processing of personal data"@en ;
    lgo:shortName "Kaderwet / GBW" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2016-679 ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2002-58 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.ejustice.just.fgov.be/eli/wet/2018/07/30/2018040581/justel> ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    rdfs:comment "Art. 10/2 (inserted by W 2021-12-21/05, art. 256, in force 10-01-2022) is Belgium's cookie rule: storage of or access to information on the terminal equipment of a subscriber or user only with clear and precise information about the purposes and rights plus consent; lid 2 is the transmission/strictly-necessary exception. It replaced art. 129 of the Wet van 13 juni 2005 betreffende de elektronische communicatie (WEC), which that law repealed; supervision moved from the BIPT to the Gegevensbeschermingsautoriteit."@en .
